KG42.register("clusters-af3ebf6a8ef02bca5e6a783d",{"id":"40-fair_dso_flexibility::v142-d-CL001","paper":"40-fair_dso_flexibility","label":"Fair flexibility allocation under security constraints and ECPM performance compensation","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL001","label":"Fair flexibility allocation under security constraints and ECPM performance compensation","market_meaning":"When expected demand cannot satisfy network constraints, the DSO performs a maximum-cost-minimization allocation based on aggregator declarations, forming flexibility instructions; at period end, ECPM payments are calculated by combining instructions, measured actions and actual cost evidence. Safe operation responsibility, allocation decisions and payment incentives jointly constitute a candidate mechanism; exact performance, incentive compatibility and positive revenue guarantees still have the following gaps.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["coordination","clearing","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The three chains belong to the same M01 mechanism and the same modeled network. The mechanism properties must retain determinism, perfect information and the original model index scope; the equivalence between the original problem and the SOCP relaxation has additional conditions. CPM is a component inherited by ECPM, and its always-perform assumption cannot directly replace the performance argument of ECPM. The uncertainty paragraph only provides a tuning discussion and does not constitute an unconditional guarantee.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The source text explicitly links declarations, the instruction of problem (11), observed results and payment calculation, and designs payment to achieve the fair allocation objective; therefore it is assembled jointly across coordination, clearing and settlement. The boundary is based on input-output and incentive relationships, not a shared DSO node; the pay-as-bid benchmark of different mechanisms is retained separately.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"It provides declaration inputs, the allocation objective, optimization decisions and the source of instructions, and is the allocation core of this mechanism."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"It provides the DSO's safe operation responsibility and voltage and current limits under the same allocation mechanism, complementing the feasibility scope of clearing."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"It uses allocation instructions and actual observations to calculate ECPM payments, and supports declaration and performance incentives through compensation and penalty design; CPM is retained as an inherited component."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-CN001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E28","v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E19"],"rationale":"The voltage and current limits in the safe operation responsibility are exactly (5)-(6) referenced by problem (11); if the network check fails, declaration and allocation are triggered. This correspondence supports the functional connection between responsibility and clearing constraints, and does not fabricate missing network constraint objects."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-CN002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::par_K_i_star","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C009"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g01-E24"],"rationale":"The optimal instruction after solving the allocation decision enters settlement and serves as the comparison benchmark for deviations in measured actions. Here the distinct roles of the decision to be solved, the obtained instruction and actual execution are retained, and these objects are not directly equated."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-CN003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T001","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T002","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T003","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::par_hatL_j","v141-c-R003::theta::par_c_j_eval","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g01-E23"],"rationale":"The same declaration system and its cost function are evaluated at other aggregators' instruction points, forming the declared cost benchmark in payment. The participant index changes with the payee; the declared cost benchmark and the payee's actual cost remain distinct."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-CN004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C010"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g01-E25","v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g03-E18"],"rationale":"The source text designs payment to induce truthful declaration and compliance with instructions, thereby achieving the allocation objective of problem (11). Here only the conditional incentive-design coupling is recorded; CPM's performance assumption and the issues between exact and approximate ECPM performance are retained, and no new scientific dependency edges are added."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g01-E28","v141-b-g01-E21"],"rationale":"The DSO in the same M01 procedure undertakes safe operation, allocation and payment design activities. The representative citation is for display only; the original node references of the three chains and all local responsibilities are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM002","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R003::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g01-E20"],"rationale":"Both places refer to the same allocation activity in which declarations solve problem (11); settlement uses the output of this activity. The display choice does not delete either original reference."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM003","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X003","v141-c-R002::x::V_sqr"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g01-E33"],"rationale":"The squared voltage quantity of the same network node and time period is used respectively for clearing decisions and for expressing safety responsibility; the local definition and constraint role remain independent."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM004","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X004","v141-c-R002::x::I_sqr"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g01-E33","v141-b-g01-E12"],"rationale":"The squared current quantity of the same line and time period. The clearing chain also involves SOC constraints, so only the physical quantity identity is associated; its local feasible region or object records are not merged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM005","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T009","v141-c-R002::theta::V_min"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g01-E32"],"rationale":"Both are the minimum voltage magnitude used by (5) in the same model; the local roles of clearing input and safety limit are retained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM006","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T008","v141-c-R002::theta::V_max"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g01-E32"],"rationale":"Both are the maximum voltage magnitude used by (5) in the same model; the identity is associated without rewriting either parameter."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM007","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T010","v141-c-R002::theta::I_max"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g01-E32"],"rationale":"Both are the maximum current magnitude of the same line in (6); the parameter records and uses of each chain are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-OM008","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E15"],"rationale":"They carry respectively the original maximum-cost-minimization model and the formulation after introducing slack variables and SOC relaxation. The source gives a conditional equivalence statement, so it is retained as an associated alternative formulation; it cannot be regarded as an unconditionally identical expression or as two independent rules."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G001","category":"unverified_source","description":"All B evidence in this cluster remains unverified. The experiment allows it to support candidate assembly, but no B-source audit, C2 independent review or Agent E check has been performed; therefore it cannot be claimed on this basis that the transcription or scientific content has been independently confirmed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g01-E28","v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g03-E15","v141-b-g03-E16","v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g03-E18"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Conduct source-text verification and independent scientific review of all supporting citations, formulas and applicable conditions, and manually check each chain and the assembly mappings in this cluster."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G002","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Clearing C003 cites (1)-(3) and (10) by number, but these network equations have not yet entered the frozen constraint catalogue as complete citable constraint objects; R002 supplements only (5)-(6). The current assembly cannot provide a complete mathematical closure of network feasibility.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X005","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X006","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E28","v141-b-g01-E29"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream C should supplement the cited power balance, voltage drop and SOC constraints and the corresponding index bindings after source-text verification; D keeps the existing objects unchanged."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G003","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The association between C005 and C003 includes replacing the original current equality with an SOC inequality. E13 only states that radial networks are equivalent under certain conditions, without listing these conditions or confirming that the current instance satisfies them; the two models cannot be unconditionally treated as having the same feasible region.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E13"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Supplement the relaxation exactness conditions cited in the source and an explanation of instance applicability; until then, keep the two formulations associated but separate."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G004","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"Network balance multiplies demand by K_{i,t}, while cost uses 1-K_{i,t}; the preceding sentence of E10 also describes 1-K_{i,t} as the changed demand proportion. The textual interpretations of load proportion and curtailment proportion conflict and propagate to the interpretation of instructions and measured actions.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004","v141-c-R003::theta::par_K_i_star","v141-c-R003::x::var_tildeK_i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E28","v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g01-E16"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the unified physical definition of K and the correspondence among demand, curtailment and cost, and have upstream clarify the text or interpretation; do not rewrite the existing formulas or quantity objects in D."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G005","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Appendix B does not retain the β coefficient from (39) to (40), nor state whether γ is rescaled; the connection between the stationary point of (41) and the demand-squared scale of (8) is not explained. The comparison between γ and λ in C010 also lacks dimensional, normalization and time-unit explanations, and cannot be directly used as an executable condition for coefficient selection.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T004","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C010","v141-c-R003::x::var_beta","v141-c-R003::x::var_gamma","v141-c-R003::theta::par_lambda_i_t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g03-E15","v141-b-g03-E16","v141-b-g03-E17"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check step by step the derivation from payment to action optimization and the stationary point, clarify β, demand scale, γ rescaling and unit conventions, then evaluate the applicable interpretation of C010; retain the frozen expressions."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G006","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Theorem 1 states that exact performance is a dominant strategy, but Appendix B ultimately obtains only approximate performance; the given stationary point for finite γ generally does not exactly coincide with the instruction. The existing content is insufficient to interpret this candidate assembly as proven exact performance and the corresponding network security guarantee.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C010"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g03-E18"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Distinguish exact and approximate incentive conclusions, clarify the error under finite γ, the action feasible region and applicable conditions, and evaluate the impact of deviations on network security constraints."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G007","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The allowable ranges and calibration procedures for β, γ and R_i are not given, and the settlement applicability boundary between measured actions and actual costs is not closed. Fixed payment ensuring positive revenue is currently a design intention; there are not yet sufficient conditions covering the allowable cost and deviation ranges.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::var_beta","v141-c-R003::x::var_gamma","v141-c-R003::x::var_R_i","v141-c-R003::x::var_tildeK_i","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E24","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g01-E16"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Clarify the allowable action, cost and parameter ranges, the exit revenue benchmark and the fixed payment calibration conditions, and check whether incentive and participation constraints can be satisfied simultaneously."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G008","category":"scope_conflict","description":"Mechanism theory presupposes determinism and perfect information; the paragraph containing uncertainty only discusses the penalty trade-off and explicitly excludes identification of deviation causes and auditing from the paper's scope. It cannot be inferred from this that the same incentive guarantees still hold under uncertainty or that default exemption rules apply.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C010","v141-c-R003::x::var_tildeK_i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should clearly distinguish deterministic theoretical properties from uncertainty tuning discussion; if the latter needs to be covered, additionally supplement risk, deviation determination and participation conditions."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G009","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The node proposals for aggregator participation, flexibility products, cost declaration, fair allocation objective, ECPM payment and incentive verification all remain pending approval. Existing generic nodes only provide functional positioning and do not mean that these specialized concepts have received ontology approval.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R003::V::settlement.payment"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g01-E26"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g01-P01","proposal:v141-b-g01-P02","proposal:v141-b-g01-P03","proposal:v141-b-g01-P04","proposal:v141-b-g01-P05","proposal:v141-b-g01-P06","v141-b-g03-P01"],"required_work":"Manually review the proposals and the relationships among duplicate participant proposals; distinguish aggregator from DSO, flexibility from local energy, and maximum-cost-minimization from social welfare objectives, and have upstream update the framework after approval."}]},"rule_refs":["40-fair_dso_flexibility::v141-c-R001","40-fair_dso_flexibility::v141-c-R002","40-fair_dso_flexibility::v141-c-R003"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-2bf6582a237ae8bd","COMP-9962fe54ff7e2f44","KG40-d5743b8980847a21"]});
